From: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:05:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/ir3: flush denormals to zero (FTZ) for ALU execution throughput

Adreno SP execution units incur significant cycle penalties when preserving
subnormal floating-point numbers. Emulators (Winlator, DXVK, VKD3D) frequently
request denorm preservation by default.

This patch forces Flush-To-Zero (FTZ) on float32 and float16 ALU operations
on A7xx to unlock maximum shader throughput.
---
 src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir.c
index 5f1234c..b821901 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir.c
@@ -218,6 +218,16 @@ ir3_optimize_loop(struct ir3_compiler *compiler, nir_shader *s)
       if (compiler->gen >= 7) {
          NIR_PASS(progress, s, nir_opt_algebraic_late);
+
+         /* Force Flush-To-Zero (FTZ) on subnormals:
+          * Removes expensive microcode exception handling on A7xx SPs.
+          */
+         nir_shader_set_fp_mode(s, (nir_fp_mode)(NIR_FP_MODE_FLUSH_TO_ZERO));
       }
 
       NIR_PASS(progress, s, nir_opt_dce);
-- 
